al, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-18)\\cdot (-2)+(-16)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4}{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-18)\\cdot (-3)+(-16)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-3)}{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373279 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5446889c-4194-56bc-877f-e62dc48f37d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373280 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\be